From: Mark Adler <git@madler.net>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 16:26:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Fix buffer overflow bug in non-blocking gzwrite.

This addresses CVE-2026-85091.

[Salvatore Bonaccorso: Backport fix to version before 81cc0bebedd9 ("Support
non-blocking devices in the gz* routines.").]
Thanks: Tobias Frost and Shafayat Hossain Majumder
---
 gzwrite.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/gzwrite.c
+++ b/gzwrite.c
@@ -241,8 +241,11 @@
                 n = (unsigned)len;
             state->strm.avail_in = n;
             state->x.pos += n;
-            if (gz_comp(state, Z_NO_FLUSH) == -1)
+            if (gz_comp(state, Z_NO_FLUSH) == -1) {
+                state->strm.avail_in = 0;
+                state->strm.next_in = state->in;
                 return 0;
+            }
             len -= n;
         } while (len);
     }
